cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use the QIDS-CAM formulation, implementation, benchmark, or derived
  architecture, please cite this software and technical report and preserve
  credit to Hayden Lindley.
title: "QIDS-CAM: Quantum-Inspired Destructive Search with Content-Addressed Memory"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lindley
    given-names: Hayden
version: 0.2.0
license: Apache-2.0
url: "https://github.com/bohselecta/corgi-qidscam"
repository-code: "https://github.com/bohselecta/corgi-qidscam"
abstract: >-
  A classical research implementation combining signed evidence cancellation,
  destructive graph pruning, context-bound learned no-goods, content-addressed
  Merkle-DAG memory, and verifiable solve receipts for graph-shaped AI reasoning.
keywords:
  - artificial intelligence
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - Merkle DAG
  - content-addressed memory
  - conflict learning
  - graph search
  - quantum-inspired computing
  - reasoning
